WEBVTT

00:00:03.600 --> 00:00:08.225
Tranche connects project milestones with protected payment decisions.

00:00:08.225 --> 00:00:11.638
This walkthrough follows a fictional client project through the

00:00:11.638 --> 00:00:15.088
real application, using the PayPal sandbox for the

00:00:15.088 --> 00:00:16.100
payment.

00:00:17.225 --> 00:00:20.825
We begin with a brief and explicit acceptance requirements

00:00:20.825 --> 00:00:21.225
.

00:00:20.938 --> 00:00:25.050
The planner generates priced milestones, tasks and dependencies

00:00:25.050 --> 00:00:26.250
for review.

00:00:26.250 --> 00:00:29.138
Nothing is sent automatically at this step.

00:00:29.138 --> 00:00:32.150
For the sandbox demonstration, we set the first

00:00:32.150 --> 00:00:35.762
milestone to one dollar and leave the website implementation

00:00:35.762 --> 00:00:38.862
as a later, unfunded milestone.

00:00:38.862 --> 00:00:42.350
The first milestone certifies only that a public endpoint

00:00:42.350 --> 00:00:44.225
responds successfully.

00:00:45.350 --> 00:00:47.762
The Gantt brings work and payment dates into the

00:00:47.762 --> 00:00:49.038
same view.

00:00:49.038 --> 00:00:52.275
Editing the first task moves the dependent work,

00:00:52.275 --> 00:00:55.038
while the milestone dates update with it.

00:00:55.038 --> 00:00:58.112
The agency can inspect the schedule before sharing the

00:00:58.112 --> 00:00:59.150
plan.

00:01:00.275 --> 00:01:02.925
The client gets a private portal with the plan

00:01:02.925 --> 00:01:05.588
, prices and acceptance criteria.

00:01:05.588 --> 00:01:10.275
The negotiation room separately configures a simulated client agent

00:01:10.275 --> 00:01:10.675
.

00:01:10.425 --> 00:01:14.100
Here, the real agent requests human review.

00:01:14.100 --> 00:01:17.275
That outcome is recorded in the transcript and appears

00:01:17.275 --> 00:01:18.812
in the review queue.

00:01:18.812 --> 00:01:21.338
The client reviews the plan and makes the next

00:01:21.338 --> 00:01:22.375
decision.

00:01:29.300 --> 00:01:33.538
After sandbox buyer approval, PayPal confirms the one-dollar

00:01:33.538 --> 00:01:35.012
authorization.

00:01:35.012 --> 00:01:38.512
The first milestone now shows an active hold.

00:01:38.512 --> 00:01:41.912
Approval and authorization are separate steps, and the

00:01:41.912 --> 00:01:44.875
money has not been released to the agency.

00:01:46.025 --> 00:01:49.150
A delivery must satisfy its machine checks.

00:01:49.150 --> 00:01:51.550
We first submit a missing page, and the

00:01:51.550 --> 00:01:53.738
availability check fails.

00:01:53.738 --> 00:01:56.400
The milestone returns for changes.

00:01:56.400 --> 00:02:00.325
Submitting the reachable endpoint creates a new verification attempt

00:02:00.325 --> 00:02:02.062
with fresh evidence.

00:02:02.062 --> 00:02:05.650
Failed checks cannot be overridden by the language model

00:02:05.650 --> 00:02:06.050
.

00:02:06.975 --> 00:02:09.975
Once the check passes and the verification proposal is

00:02:09.975 --> 00:02:13.812
reviewed, the milestone becomes ready for release.

00:02:13.812 --> 00:02:17.100
The client can keep manual release or configure a

00:02:17.100 --> 00:02:20.075
rule that applies after verification.

00:02:20.075 --> 00:02:23.762
In this demonstration, the client explicitly releases the

00:02:23.762 --> 00:02:27.800
first milestone, and PayPal confirms the capture.

00:02:28.950 --> 00:02:32.612
The cash flow dashboard separates held, released,

00:02:32.612 --> 00:02:35.125
overdue and forecast amounts.

00:02:35.125 --> 00:02:38.350
Agent activity provides a reviewable history, and the

00:02:38.350 --> 00:02:42.088
assistant helps explore the dashboard without approving actions or

00:02:42.088 --> 00:02:43.388
moving money.

00:02:43.388 --> 00:02:47.050
The remaining website milestone is still unfunded.

00:02:47.050 --> 00:02:50.525
Tranche keeps the plan, evidence and payment decisions

00:02:50.525 --> 00:02:51.600
connected.
